<!--
  presentation-watchdog.plist.template -- rendered by install_watchdog_schedule()
  in lib-presentation-schedules.sh (F12a), which install.sh (Step 6.6c) and
  update-skills.sh (every roll) both call. It replaces every <...> placeholder
  below, adds the environment launchd does not supply, and writes the rendered
  copy to ~/Library/LaunchAgents/com.blackceo.presentation-watchdog.plist on Mac
  (Linux/VPS gets a */10 SILENT main-session openclaw cron running the same
  script instead -- there is no launchd in the container).

  THIS FILE USED TO SAY "ready-to-apply, NOT installed -- Named Stop". That was
  true and it was the whole problem: nothing installed it, so on every client box
  presentation-watchdog.sh's four passes -- stall watchdog, board reconcile,
  SUPERVISOR (engine-liveness restart) and run-discovery -- were dead code, and
  every stalled deck run needed a human to notice it. Measured at v25.0.11 with
  python3 str.count over the full file text: 'presentation-watchdog' appeared 0
  times in install.sh and 0 times in update-skills.sh, against a same-instrument
  'presentation-intake-poll' control of 25 in install.sh.

  PLACEHOLDERS install_watchdog_schedule() replaces:
    1. <WATCHDOG_SCRIPT_PATH>  -- absolute path to presentation-watchdog.sh
    2. <SCAN_ROOT>             -- the run root to scan (the department's runs/)
    3. <LOG_PATH>              -- where stdout/stderr go. This SAME path is
                                  passed as argv[2], because the script tees its
                                  own diagnostics into the file it is handed and
                                  the launchd log and the script log must be one
                                  file.

  ENVIRONMENT THE RENDERER ADDS (not placeholders -- launchd hands a job
  essentially NO environment, and these are resolved per box, never guessed):
    PATH                       -- launchd supplies none, so python3, gtimeout and
                                  the openclaw CLI the notify transport execs are
                                  all invisible without this.
    PRESENTATION_NOTIFY_CMD    -- the co-located transport, and ONLY if the file
                                  exists. presentation-watchdog.sh is FAIL-CLOSED
                                  on an unusable transport (exit 4,
                                  AF-NOTIFY-UNCONFIGURED) and refuses the whole
                                  pass, so this renders EMPTY rather than point at
                                  a missing file -- empty is safe because the
                                  script loads the box env store itself
                                  (presentation_job/env_store.py) before that gate.
    OPENCLAW_ROOT / OPENCLAW_WORKSPACE_PATH / OPENCLAW_WORKSPACE_ROOT
                               -- so the env store resolves this client's stores
                                  and not another installation's.
    OWNER_CHAT_ID              -- the NUMERIC owner chat id, resolved from
                                  $OWNER_CHAT_ID, $OPENCLAW_OWNER_CHAT_ID or the
                                  owner target install.sh already resolved.
                                  report.py's resolve_subsystem_chat() swaps a
                                  subsystem NAME (watchdog/supervisor/capacity)
                                  for it; without it a stall alert has nowhere to
                                  land. Renders EMPTY when nothing answers -- an
                                  id is never invented.
    PRESENTATION_SUPERVISE_APPLY
                               -- ABSENT by default: the supervisor pass runs
                                  REPORT-ONLY. Arming it (F12c) is gated on F2
                                  (auto-repin on manifest change) being deployed,
                                  because until then the supervisor's restart is a
                                  --resume that dies on the manifest pin and burns
                                  its 3-restart budget in ~30 minutes. The
                                  renderer sets it only when the operator exports
                                  it, and PRESERVES a value already present in an
                                  installed plist so a roll can neither arm what
                                  an operator did not nor disarm what they did.

  The Label stays com.presentations.watchdog even though the installed FILE is
  com.blackceo.presentation-watchdog.plist: that is what this fleet already
  carries (verified on the operator Mac 2026-09-06 -- that filename on disk, this
  Label inside, and `launchctl list` showing it loaded with status 0). launchd
  keys on the LABEL, so rendering onto the existing filename heals that box
  instead of colliding with it.

  Uninstall (Named Stop -- do not run unattended):
    launchctl unload ~/Library/LaunchAgents/com.blackceo.presentation-watchdog.plist
    rm ~/Library/LaunchAgents/com.blackceo.presentation-watchdog.plist

  Verify it is loaded:
    launchctl list | grep com.presentations.watchdog
-->
<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN"
  "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
    <key>Label</key>
    <string>com.presentations.watchdog</string>
    <key>ProgramArguments</key>
    <array>
        <string>/bin/sh</string>
        <string>&lt;WATCHDOG_SCRIPT_PATH&gt;</string>
        <string>&lt;LOG_PATH&gt;</string>
    </array>
    <key>EnvironmentVariables</key>
    <dict>
        <key>SCAN_ROOT</key>
        <string>&lt;SCAN_ROOT&gt;</string>
        <key>GRACE</key>
        <string>1.5</string>
        <key>SCAN_DEPTH</key>
        <string>3</string>
    </dict>
    <key>StartInterval</key>
    <integer>600</integer>
    <key>RunAtLoad</key>
    <false/>
    <key>StandardOutPath</key>
    <string>&lt;LOG_PATH&gt;</string>
    <key>StandardErrorPath</key>
    <string>&lt;LOG_PATH&gt;</string>
</dict>
</plist>
